c-number>1025113</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-8201698-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8201698</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> <patcit ucid="WO-1999027532-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>WO</country> <doc-number>1999027532</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="AE" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>NIKKEI ELECTRONICS no. 718, 15 June 1998, pages 48 - 50, XP002923157</text><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1020853A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUBOTA SHIGEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SONY CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE KENJIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUBOTA, SHIGEO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SONY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, KENJIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUBOTA SHIGEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE KENJIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUBOTA, SHIGEO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, KENJIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A catadioptric lens preferable when evanescent light is used and having substantially no coma. The catadioptric lens has first surface (S1) which is a concave refractive surface, a second surface (S2) which is a plane mirror, and a third surface (S3) which is a concave aspherical mirror coaxial with the first surface (S1). Incident parallel light is focused on the total reflection surface of a fourth surface (S4) through an opening provided in the second surface (S2). The radius of curvature of the first surface (S1) and the optical length d from the first surface (S1) to the vertex of the third surface (S3) are so determined as to satisfy the sine condition.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Lentille catadioptrique mise en application, de préférence, avec de la lumière évanescente et ne présentant pratiquement aucun coma. Cette lentille catadioptrique possède une première surface (S1) qui est une surface de réfraction concave, une deuxième surface (S2) qui consiste en un miroir plan et une troisième surface (S3) qui consiste en un miroir concave asphérique situé dans le même axe que la première surface (S1). La lumière parallèle incidente est concentrée sur la totalité de la zone de réflexion d'une quatrième surface (S4) à travers une ouverture située dans la deuxième surface (S2). Le rayon d'incurvation de la première surface (S1) et la longueur optique d depuis la première surface (S1) jusqu'au vertex de la troisième surface (S3) sont déterminés de façon à répondre à la condition du sinus.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>